Rust (native)Python (drop-in) <pre><code>use spark_connect::{SparkSession, functions as f};

let spark = SparkSession::builder()
    .remote("sc://localhost:15002")
    .get_or_create()?;
spark.range(100)?.select([f::col("id")]).show(20)?;
</code></pre> <pre><code>from pyspark.sql import SparkSession, functions as sf

spark = SparkSession.builder.remote("sc://localhost:15002").getOrCreate()
spark.range(0, 100).select(sf.col("id")).show(20)
</code></pre> <p>Both paths build the same protobuf plan through the same Rust core and get the same Arrow results back. The Python package is a compatibility skin over <code>pyspark-rs</code>; it does not fork or reimplement the client logic.</p>
